#: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:fool}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1988|author=w:Larry Kramer|title=Just Say No|passage=What do you mean, since when did I become such a radical fairy? Since I started knowing '''twits''' like you, you '''twit'''!}}
# {{lb|en|British|dialectal|archaic}} A person who [[chatter#Verb|chatters]] or [[gossip#Verb|gossips]] [[inanely]]; a [[chatterer]], a [[gossip#Noun|gossip]] or [[gossiper]]; also, a person who  [[divulge]]s [[private#Adjective|private]] [[information]] about others or is [[indiscreet]]; a [[tattletale#Noun|tattletale]].
#: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:gossiper}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In Australia, Britain, Ireland, Australia, and New Zealand, {{senseno|en|fool}} (“annoying or foolish person”) is usually used in an affectionate or humorous manner.

